## Product behavior

- Nav tab after AEO/GEO: **Exhibit G — Live Jobs**
- Roles: **AI + software only**
- Talent bench: 4 slots — `ai_1`, `ai_2`, `software_1`, `software_2` (PDF/DOCX upload; matching can stay empty until resumes exist)
- Scan: prefer jobs **posted ≤ 30 minutes**; if fewer than 12, **fill from last 60 minutes** up to 20 jobs. Never show days/weeks/months-old JDs.
- Outreach: **copy-ready draft** only (clipboard + optional mailto). Does **not** log in or send LinkedIn/Naukri messages.
- Optional: paste a public LinkedIn `/jobs/view/` or Naukri `/job-listings` URL (`POST /api/live-jobs/ingest`)

## Discovery (this was the working version)

- **Primary:** LinkedIn public guest search (no login):
  `https://www.linkedin.com/jobs-guest/jobs/api/seeMoreJobPostings/search?keywords=...&f_TPR=r3600&start=0|10`
- Keywords: software engineer, machine learning engineer, AI engineer, python developer, full stack developer, data scientist, backend engineer, generative AI
- Parse `div.base-card` / `div.job-search-card`: title, company, `a[href*=/jobs/view/]`, `<time>` relative text first (`14 minutes ago`), then `datetime`
- Do **not** fetch LinkedIn job detail pages (authwall strips time)
- If LinkedIn card has no parsed age, treat as 60 minutes because `f_TPR=r3600` is already past hour
- **Naukri:** public jobapi is captcha-walled; DDG `site:naukri.com/job-listings "..."` is secondary and usually thin. Be honest in UI copy.
- **Do not** use DuckDuckGo `site:linkedin.com/jobs/view ("minutes ago" OR "just now")` — that returns zero live jobs

## APIs (wire exactly)

- `GET /api/talent-bench`
- `POST /api/talent-bench/upload?slot_id=ai_1` (multipart `file`)
- `DELETE /api/talent-bench/{slot_id}`
- `POST /api/live-jobs/scan` `{ "minutes": 30, "sources": ["linkedin","naukri"] }`
- `POST /api/live-jobs/ingest` `{ "url": "..." }`
- `POST /api/live-jobs/outreach` `{ "job": {...}, "slot_id": "ai_1"|null }`

Scan response includes `jobs`, `window_minutes`, `fallback_used`, `in_window_count`, `_meta.note`.

Job recency labels: `posted_in_window` | `posted_in_fallback`. Sort freshest first. Cap `MAX_JOBS = 20`.

